---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
const sections = [
  { title: 'Your data and their models', items: [
    'Is customer data used to train or fine-tune models, and can that be switched off in writing, not only in a settings toggle',
    'Which third-party model providers see your data (OpenAI, Anthropic, Google, others) and under what terms',
    'How long prompts, uploads and outputs are retained, and whether zero-retention is available',
    'Which region the data is processed and stored in, and whether you can pin it',
    'Whether data is encrypted at rest and in transit, and who holds the keys',
    'What happens to your data when you cancel: deletion timeline, export format, written confirmation',
  ]},
  { title: 'Access and identity', items: [
    'Single sign-on (SAML or OIDC) available on the tier you are buying, not only the enterprise tier',
    'Role-based permissions that separate admins, editors and viewers',
    'Audit log of who did what, exportable, kept for at least a year',
    'Multi-factor authentication enforced for all users, including API keys',
    'API keys can be scoped and rotated without downtime',
  ]},
  { title: 'Compliance and paperwork', items: [
    'Current SOC 2 Type II or ISO 27001 report, dated within the last 12 months, available under NDA',
    'A data processing agreement you can sign, with a named list of subprocessors and change notifications',
    'GDPR, UK GDPR or CCPA position stated for your jurisdiction, with a named DPO or privacy contact',
    'Penetration test summary from the last 12 months',
    'Breach notification commitment in hours, written into the contract',
    'Cyber insurance in place, with a stated coverage amount',
  ]},
  { title: 'How the AI behaves', items: [
    'A human can review, edit or reject AI output before it reaches a customer or a record of truth',
    'Sources or citations shown for factual answers, so you can check them',
    'Known failure modes documented: what it gets wrong, how often, and what the vendor measured',
    'You own the outputs, and the contract says so',
    'Prompt injection and data leakage between customers are addressed in their security documentation',
    'Model changes are announced ahead of time, with a way to test before they roll out',
  ]},
  { title: 'Commercial and exit', items: [
    'Uptime commitment with credits, and a public status page with history',
    'Support response times by severity, in writing',
    'Price change notice period of at least 60 days, and a cap at renewal',
    'Full export of your data and configuration in an open format, tested during the trial',
    'Termination for convenience, or at worst a short notice period after the first term',
  ]},
];
const total = sections.reduce((n, s) => n + s.items.length, 0);
---
<Base title="AI vendor security and data checklist: what to ask before you buy" description="A checklist of the security, data handling, compliance and exit questions to ask any software or AI vendor before signing. Tick items in your browser, copy it into your review, print it.">
  <section class="hero">
    <p class="meta"><a href="/learn/">Learn</a> / checklist</p>
    <h1>AI vendor security and data checklist</h1>
    <p class="lead">{total} questions in five groups. Most vendors answer the first group in their security page and go quiet on the last. Progress is saved in this browser only. Copy the text into your vendor review or print it for the call.</p>
    <div class="row">
      <span class="pill" id="progress">0 of {total} confirmed</span>
      <button class="btn ghost" type="button" id="reset">Reset</button>
      <button class="btn ghost" type="button" id="copy">Copy as text</button>
      <button class="btn ghost" type="button" onclick="window.print()">Print</button>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section prose" id="checklist">
    {sections.map((s, si) => (
      <div class="check-group">
        <h2 style={si === 0 ? 'margin-top:0' : ''}>{s.title}</h2>
        <ul class="checklist">
          {s.items.map((item, ii) => {
            const id = `v-${si}-${ii}`;
            return (
              <li>
                <label class="check-item" for={id}>
                  <input type="checkbox" id={id} data-key={id} />
                  <span>{item}</span>
                </label>
              </li>
            );
          })}
        </ul>
      </div>
    ))}
  </section>

  <section class="section prose">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">What a good answer looks like</h2>
    <p>A vendor that has done this before sends a trust page, a SOC 2 report under NDA and a DPA within a day, and answers the model training question with a sentence, not a paragraph. A vendor that has not will ask you to get on a call. Neither is a deal breaker for a small purchase, but the pattern tells you how they will behave when something goes wrong.</p>
    <p>Score the result in the data handling row of the <a href="/learn/tool-evaluation-scorecard/">evaluation scorecard</a>. Firms writing an internal policy for AI use can start from the <a href="/blog/chatgpt-policy-for-accounting-firms/">policy article</a>, which applies well beyond accounting.</p>
  </section>

  <script>
    const KEY = 'lantle-vendor-checklist';
    const boxes = Array.from(document.querySelectorAll<HTMLInputElement>('input[type=checkbox][data-key]'));
    const progress = document.getElementById('progress');
    const load = (): Record<string, boolean> => { try { return JSON.parse(localStorage.getItem(KEY) || '{}'); } catch { return {}; } };
    const save = (state: Record<string, boolean>) => { try { localStorage.setItem(KEY, JSON.stringify(state)); } catch {} };
    const render = () => {
      const done = boxes.filter((b) => b.checked).length;
      if (progress) progress.textContent = `${done} of ${boxes.length} confirmed`;
    };
    const state = load();
    boxes.forEach((b) => { b.checked = !!state[b.dataset.key!]; b.addEventListener('change', () => { state[b.dataset.key!] = b.checked; save(state); render(); }); });
    render();
    document.getElementById('reset')?.addEventListener('click', () => { boxes.forEach((b) => (b.checked = false)); save({}); render(); });
    document.getElementById('copy')?.addEventListener('click', async () => {
      const lines: string[] = [];
      document.querySelectorAll('.check-group').forEach((g) => {
        lines.push(g.querySelector('h2')?.textContent ?? '', ...Array.from(g.querySelectorAll('.check-item')).map((l) => `- [${(l.querySelector('input') as HTMLInputElement).checked ? 'x' : ' '}] ${l.querySelector('span')?.textContent}`), '');
      });
      try { await navigator.clipboard.writeText(lines.join('\n')); const btn = document.getElementById('copy'); if (btn) btn.textContent = 'Copied'; } catch {}
    });
  </script>
</Base>
